ning labia to its  destiny  but once the old master gaddafi was dead  the race for the libyan resources had  just begun u.s sources stressed to the  various departments the importance of  not allowing countries such as turkey or  italy to invade the field designated for  u.s france and qatar the death of  gaddafi aroused the mixed reactions in  libya there were those who rejoiced  those who were still attached to the  memory of the old leader and those who  knew that the future crisis would make  the old regime be regretted what  resulted from the fall of gaddafi was  dictated by the historical dualism that  separated tsrinika and tripolitania a  polarization that led to a de facto  separation in two of libya with the rise  of islamist groups and small local gangs  around 300 of them and with a breakup of  the old alliances between the various  tribes in the southern part of the  country libya turned into anarchy where  no one was actually in power anymore and  where everyone had its own interest  history teaches us that libya has been  torn by two civil wars the first ended  with the death of gaddafi in october  2011 and the second began in 2014 and  still ongoing the truth is that the war  has never ended it always went on and  from the arab spring libya moved to the  arab winter on one hand there were the  national forces loyal to general after  who had settled down in cyronaica in  tobruk he soon stood out as the strong  man in charge with the claim that the  general national congress mandate was  expired after was backed and financed by  the united arab emirates egypt saudi  arabia france syria and russia on the  other hand there was a whole series of  various forces in tripolitania under the  umbrella of the government of national  accord whose ex-prime minister al-saraj  was accused by haftar of terrorism from  2012 this side was supported by turkey  the us and the european union basically  al-saraj blamed after for his purpose to  bring back a qadhafi style 